{"index":3401,"node_id":"5b5f36e7-3806-46e8-97eb-d90f56f02886","parent":"3ab2ca08-a275-4984-854b-f902fcd109a1","role":"assistant","author_name":null,"create_time":1791165585.714378,"update_time":1791165602.716914,"content_type":"text","status":"finished_successfully","end_turn":true,"recipient":"all","model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","default_model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","part":1,"parts_total":1,"text":"Correct. I described it incorrectly.\n\nYou asked for a **one-level unwrap**, not general flattening:\n\n```json\n{\"metadata\":{\n  \"this\":\"metadata\",\n  \"file_description\":\"...\",\n  \"metadata_region\":{\n    \"length\":16384,\n    \"padding_character\":\"~\",\n    \"body_start\":16384,\n    \"coordinate_unit\":\"UTF-16_code_unit\"\n  }\n}}\n```\n\nbecomes:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"this\":\"metadata\",\n  \"file_description\":\"...\",\n  \"metadata_region\":{\n    \"length\":16384,\n    \"padding_character\":\"~\",\n    \"body_start\":16384,\n    \"coordinate_unit\":\"UTF-16_code_unit\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n`metadata_region` and any future nested objects **stay nested exactly as they are**. Only the redundant outer `\"metadata\"` parent disappears.\n\nAnd the actual document was still showing that redundant parent, so that part was **not yet complete**. fileciteturn829file0L2-L5"}
